      "sha256": "bbb98200f52b4a692ce097704b8c438179a795a44bec6b856c03cf31931af4ea",
      "reason": "The model–WOA23 correlations, RMSEs and basin/global comparisons must use one common mask over all four fields and only cells where every field has data, as the fragment requires.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Build one shared valid-data mask for all four regridded nitracline fields with `build_comparison_mask` and apply it with `.where(mask)` before the correlation and RMSE; `ocean_only=True` (default) is right here because WOA23 is the reference.",
        "A mask built on one level does not carry to another: build the shared mask from the nitracline-depth fields themselves, not from a surface mask, and report the mask cell counts."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "basin-and-region-definitions",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "methods/basin-and-region-definitions.md",
      "sha256": "d0d90c32fab9f6e0a39d4f769a4e902e6412b2ad1b09d9c7d19f6bb3aa426611",
      "reason": "Basin means depend on the chosen basin partition, so the answer must state that it uses the WOA23 basin mask with marginal seas folded into parent oceans and Southern/Arctic excluded.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Use the WOA23 basin mask via `select_basin`/`load_basin_mask` with `include_marginal_seas=True` (default) to fold marginal seas into their parent ocean, and `depth_dependent=False` for surface labels applied through the whole column; state that a WOA labelling is used, not the OMIP 10-region mask, and whether marginal seas are folded.",
        "The Ofx `basin` field is not in the local archive, so basin means must come from the WOA23 mask carried onto each grid."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "omip-native-grid-vs-regridded",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "methods/omip-native-grid-vs-regridded.md",
      "sha256": "8ff046ffbadc5794fcd2f8fe93d3bb947c736dec650aa3a3cd6e2412b7da8e68",
      "reason": "The nitracline should be computed on each model’s own grid and regridded only for WOA23-grid maps and pattern comparisons, since regridding changes masks and exactness.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Compute global and basin mean nitracline depths on each source's own grid with its own `areacello`; regrid to the WOA 1° grid only for the maps, the pattern correlation and the RMSE, using `regrid_horizontal` method 'conservative' going coarser, and state the method.",
        "Nitracline depth is quantised by the vertical grid and the products' levels differ, so locate the maximum gradient on each profile's own levels; do not select a nearest common level."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cmip6-bgc-units-per-volume",
      "severity": "must",
      "path": "concepts/cmip6-bgc-units-per-volume.md",
      "sha256": "30d729792e1986dd91c822785512ceabe336ef10a47f0a7db602802e5425d70b",
      "reason": "CMIP6 nitrate is stored per unit volume while WOA23 nitrate is per unit mass, so the nitrate fields must be converted to a common unit before gradients and shared-unit sections.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Model `no3` is mol m-3 and WOA23 is µmol kg-1: convert with in-situ density (`compute_potential_density_anomaly`, `ref_pressure=None`) to put Figure 2's panels on one concentration unit, and state `attrs['density_assumption']`.",
        "Nitracline depth itself is scale-invariant: no conversion is needed, since a constant density cancels exactly (in-situ density would shift the located depth slightly)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cmip6-grid-labels",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "datasets/cmip6-grid-labels.md",
      "sha256": "e349f9e305621b6c10b35cccd0490da521cc7e3ba08bfb53890479f81024d117",
      "reason": "GFDL-ESM4 is provided as gr rather than gn, and the gn/gr distinction affects masks, exact operations and interpretation of the “native grid” nitracline.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "GFDL-ESM4 is `gr` (already remapped to 1° with conserve_order1), so its \"native\" numbers are on its 1° archive grid; CESM2 (~100 km) and MPI (~250 km) differ in resolution, so narrow features are not comparably resolved."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "omip-weighted-means-and-integrals",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "methods/omip-weighted-means-and-integrals.md",
      "sha256": "89de52676ae54db8f5897bc77a08c78de3f776696db0020935a38b790c302cbe",
      "reason": "Global and basin means must use explicit OMIP-style area weighting with every valid grid point, not unweighted cell averages.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Every global and basin mean must be area-weighted (`compute_basic_stat`, `op='area_weighted_mean'`), with weights restricted to the same valid cells; `compute_difference_metrics` weights by area by default and `analyze_correlation` needs `weighting='area'`.",
        "An unweighted `mean()` over the map counts a polar cell as heavily as a tropical one, so it is wrong for these means."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "monthly-means-are-time-averages",
      "severity": "must",
      "path": "pitfalls/monthly-means-are-time-averages.md",
      "sha256": "df6b5c23460f88f1522e5c6a665e1efbb8322c3ae876c885530f3019aa284ee0",
      "reason": "Nitracline depth is a nonlinear diagnostic, so computing it offline from monthly means or a monthly-mean climatology may differ from an online diagnostic and must be treated as such.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "The nitracline is a nonlinear diagnostic of monthly means: average first, then locate the maximum gradient, because the WOA23 reference is a climatology and this is the like-for-like choice; state the order used.",
        "Average the 1971–2000 monthly fields with `temporal_aggregate`, which uses day weights in the model calendar; an equal-weight average of monthly means is not a time average."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "missing-values-and-land-cells",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "pitfalls/missing-values-and-land-cells.md",
      "sha256": "f576244f13dde06fed1777eaa9721c68844f61758f66fac704b44f1551e90df2",
      "reason": "CMIP6 land and below-sea-floor cells are marked with 1e20, so they must be masked before computing gradients, maps or means to avoid silently dominating the results.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "xarray decodes 1e20 to NaN; build each field's valid mask from the field itself (masks differ between variables of one model) and mask the weights to those cells — a hand-rolled weighted sum returns 0.0 at land.",
        "A value near 1e20 in any output is an unmasked fill value, not a result."
      ]
    }
